Animated wallpapers were not animating because `backgroundPosition` was set as an inline style, overriding the CSS animation due to specificity rules.

## Changes

- **`buildWallpaperStyle()`**: Added `animationsEnabled` parameter; conditionally omits `backgroundPosition` from inline styles when true
- **`getWallpaperSelection()`**: Passes `settings.animationsEnabled` to style builder
- **CSS**: Added initial `background-position` to `.wallpaper-animate` class to set animation starting point

```typescript
// Before: backgroundPosition always set inline (blocks animation)
const buildWallpaperStyle = (wallpaper: WallpaperDefinition): CSSProperties => ({
  backgroundImage: `...`,
  backgroundPosition: `center, 0 0, 40px 20px`, // ❌ Overrides animation
})

// After: conditionally omit when animating
const buildWallpaperStyle = (wallpaper: WallpaperDefinition, animationsEnabled: boolean): CSSProperties => {
  const style = { backgroundImage: `...` }
  if (!animationsEnabled) {
    style.backgroundPosition = `...` // ✅ Static positioning only
  }
  return style
}
```

When animations are enabled, CSS keyframes now control background position. When disabled, inline styles preserve static positioning.

