The preview displayed with unwanted zoom effect, showing only a portion of the document instead of fitting naturally within the scrollable card container.

## Root Cause

The `applyZoom()` function applied `transform: scale(1)` and fixed container height even at 100% zoom, overriding the natural CSS layout (max-height + overflow-y) intended for the preview card.

## Changes

- **Modified `applyZoom()` in `js/ui.js`**: Clear all zoom-related inline styles at 100% zoom
  - Remove `transform`, `transform-origin` from preview element
  - Remove fixed `height` from container
  - Allows CSS max-height (600px) and overflow scrolling to work naturally
  - Preserves scale transform and calculated height for non-100% zoom levels

```javascript
applyZoom(element) {
    if (this.currentZoom === 100) {
        // Clear styles - let natural CSS handle layout
        element.style.transform = '';
        element.style.transformOrigin = '';
        const container = element.parentElement;
        if (container) {
            container.style.height = '';
        }
    } else {
        // Apply zoom transform as before
        element.style.transform = `scale(${this.currentZoom / 100})`;
        // ... calculate container height
    }
}
```

## Screenshots

**Before:** Preview constrained to fixed 402px height with scale transform
![Before fix](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0fb6f863-ce3e-480a-beab-c050e7ede09b)

**After:** Preview uses natural CSS layout with scrolling
![After fix](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a7342fdb-65ec-4b9a-b253-561a7a9d8ee7)

Zoom in/out/reset functionality remains intact.

